topics.body:
Core and Pro licence holders: the full library from the private GitHub repository wunder-ui/wunderui-core (Polar invites your GitHub account after the purchase). The npm package of the same name is WunderUI Free (free components only).

Accept the GitHub invitation, `git clone https://github.com/wunder-ui/wunderui-core`, run `npm install && npm run build` in it once, then in your project: `mkdir .wunderui`, `npm pack <wunderui-core>/packages/react --pack-destination .wunderui` and `npm install ./.wunderui/<the .tgz>`. The wunderui-setup agent skill does all of it.

`npm install @wunderui/react` installs WunderUI Free from npm: the free components only (no charts, data tables, AI or agent components). Core and Pro need the full library from the private wunderui-core repository — never install the npm package for them. Free plan: the 89 free components are MIT source at https://github.com/wunder-ui/wunderui — add them with `npx wunderui-cli add <name>` (files, dependencies and styles), install the Free package with `npm install @wunderui/react`, or copy components/, lib/ and styles/wunderui.css (each free component in design.json has a sourceRaw URL). Core and Pro components come with a plan (https://wunderui.com/#pricing).

Then wire up the styles and import:

```css
/* your Tailwind entry point */
@import "tailwindcss";
@import "@wunderui/react/styles.css";
@source "../node_modules/@wunderui/react/dist";
```

